From a8100ae355b863e560682ee1f9f3b0602e4e5c33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:27:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][3D] Automatic decides HDR in 3D for each display, by
 what Check this setup found there

Nothing a display sends says whether it takes HDR in 3D: an EDID says
what it takes in 2D, and a projector that takes HDR10 refused the 3D
mode of an HDR10 picture ("3D settings are not supported in HDR
video"). "How 3D video goes out" (videoscreen.hades3dcolour) sends SDR
at Automatic since the last change. It now decides for each display:

- Until "Check this setup" has found it on a display (its card "3D:
  HDR", in the settings add-on), Automatic sends SDR, which every 3D
  display shows, in BT.2020 where the display declares BT.2020 in its
  EDID and the driver can send it, else in BT.709
  (SdrMappedContainer() decides it, and says why where BT.709 goes
  out). An HDR film's colours are BT.2020, and the colour space is part
  of every SDR signal: no HDR signalling goes out.
- What the check found is kept for each display, by the make and model
  of its EDID, in special://profile/hades-3d-hdr.txt, as the mode of
  the menus of each display is (DisplayModeMemory.h): "hdr" (the
  display showed HDR in 3D: Automatic sends HDR there), "sdr" (it did
  not: SDR). It is read again as each video starts, for the display
  that plays it; another display's answer is never taken.
- On a display that takes HDR, where it was not checked, the first HDR
  3D video that goes out as SDR tells the user once (the display is
  then kept as "told") where to check it. kodi.log says what Automatic
  sent, on which display, and why.
- The player information says it in the row of the 3D output: "HDR in
  3D not checked yet", "checked: HDR works" or "checked: no HDR in 3D".
  It publishes the key
  of the display (hades.out.displaykey), which the check keeps its
  answer by.
- HDR, SDR in BT.2020 and SDR in BT.709 do what they did, whatever
  the check found. The help of the setting says all of it in plain
  words.

Strings: core #62871 and #62872, Estuary #54930 to #54934 and the help
(#62601, #54601), in English and in the three Spanish translations of
Estuary. The pages for other skins (system/hades) are made again from
Estuary's files.
